# carry-drift.ratchet -- pairs that had ALREADY drifted on the day the guard
# was written. See bin/carry-drift.sh.
#
# SHRINKS ONLY. `--accept` drops rows whose pair now matches; it will not add
# one. Growing this file is a hand edit, on purpose, so that it is reviewed --
# and there is no good reason to: the fix is one command, `carry-drift.sh
# --carry <bashified checkout>`, and the only thing that makes it a decision
# rather than a formality is that four of these five are LINTS every self-dev
# account runs, so re-carrying them changes what those accounts enforce. That
# is its own change with its own review: hf7y/realisateur#342.
#
# SEEDED 2026-08-16 against origin/bashified at 8504b21, main at b79d681.
# Rows are `pair <path on bashified> <path on main>`.
